 34CL c  1978Ba61,1978Ba77: 13 and 14.6-MeV |a beams from the 7.5-MV Van de     
 34CL2c  Graaff accelerator at the Strasbourg Nuclear Research Center, France,  
 34CL3c  on a 200-|mg/cm{+2} red phosphorus target. |g rays were detected using 
 34CL4c  two Ge(Li) detectors. Measured |g(|q). Deduced mixing ratios, lifetimes
 34CL5c  using RDM.                                                             
 34CL c  1978Ba39: 14.4-MeV |a beams from the 7.5-MV Van de Graaff accelerator  
 34CL2c  at the Strasbourg Nuclear Research Center, France, on a 200-|mg/cm{+2} 
 34CL3c  red phosphorus target. Neutrons were detected using a NE213 liquid     
 34CL4c  scintillator. |g rays were detected using a Ge(Li) detector. Measured  
 34CL5c  n|g-coin. 1978Ba39 is primarily a {+27}Al({+12}C,|an|g)34CL reaction   
 34CL6c  measurement.                                                           
 34CL c  1971Ba98: 0.3-0.7 MeV>threshold |a beams from the Padova 5.5 MV Van de 
 34CL2c  Graaff generator. Targets were 100-|mg/cm{+3} evaporated Zn{-3}P{-2}.  
 34CL3c  |g rays were detected using a 55-cm{+3} Ge(li) detector. Deduced       
 34CL4c  lifetimes using RDM.                                                   
 34CL c  1970Br10: 7.50-8.75-MeV |a beam on a 600-|mg/cm{+2} red phosphorus     
 34CL2c  target. |g rays were detected using a Ge(Li) detector. Deduced         
 34CL3c  lifetimes using DSAM. Also measured |g-ray angular distributions in    
 34CL4c  {+32}S({+3}He,p|g){+34}Cl reaction.                                    
